{"name":"Emperor Jade","hex":"#007b75","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"emperor","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The male monarch or ruler of an empire.","Any monarch ruling an empire, irrespective of gender, with \"empress\" contrasting to mean the consort of an emperor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emperor"},{"term":"jade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A semiprecious stone, either nephrite or jadeite, generally green or white in color, often used for carving figurines.","A bright shade of slightly bluish or greyish green, typical of polished jade stones."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a grayish shade of green, typical of jade stones."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jade Emperor","blocks":[{"text":"In the myths and folk religion of Chinese culture, the Jade Emperor or Yudi is one of the representations of the primordial god."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/%E7%8E%89%E7%9A%87%E5%A4%A7%E5%B8%9D%E7%95%AB%E5%83%8F.jpg/330px-%E7%8E%89%E7%9A%87%E5%A4%A7%E5%B8%9D%E7%95%AB%E5%83%8F.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jade_Emperor"},{"title":"Emperor","blocks":[{"text":"An emperor is the (male) ruler of an empire. Empress, the female equivalent, may indicate an emperor's wife, mother/grandmother, or a woman who rules in her own right and name. Emperors are generally recognised to be of the highest monarchic honour and rank, surpassing kings. In Europe, the title of Emperor has been used since the Middle Ages, considered in those times equal or almost equal in dignity to that of Pope due to the latter's position as visible head of the Church and spiritual leader of the Catholic part of Western Europe. The emperor of Japan is the only currently reigning monarch whose title is translated into English as \"Emperor\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Emperor_Naruhito_and_Empress_Masako_20190515.jpg/330px-Emperor_Naruhito_and_Empress_Masako_20190515.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor"},{"title":"Jade","blocks":[{"text":"Jade is an umbrella term for two different types of decorative rocks used for jewelry or ornaments. Jade is often referred to by either of two different silicate mineral names: nephrite, or jadeite. Nephrite is typically green, although it may be yellow, white or black. Jadeite varies from white or near-colorless, through various shades of green, to lavender, yellow, orange, brown and black. Rarely it may be blue. Both of these names refer to their use as gemstones, and each has a mineralogically more specific name. Both the amphibole jade (nephrite) and pyroxene jade are mineral aggregates (rocks) rather than mineral species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Jadestein.jpg/330px-Jadestein.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jade"},{"title":"Shades of green","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color green may differ in hue, chroma or lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a green or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Shades_of_Green.svg/330px-Shades_of_Green.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_green"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Jade_Emperor._Ming_Dynasty.jpg/500px-Jade_Emperor._Ming_Dynasty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Jade_Emperor._Ming_Dynasty.jpg/500px-Jade_Emperor._Ming_Dynasty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Portrait of the Jade Emperor, 16th century, Ming dynasty (Museum of Fine Arts, Boston)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJade_Emperor._Ming_Dynasty.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Jiacun_Double-Fourth_Temple_Festival_in_May_2016_02.jpg/500px-Jiacun_Double-Fourth_Temple_Festival_in_May_2016_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Jiacun_Double-Fourth_Temple_Festival_in_May_2016_02.jpg/500px-Jiacun_Double-Fourth_Temple_Festival_in_May_2016_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ritual participants carry the statue of Jade Emperor in a sedan chair at a sacrificial procession in Shanxi, 2016.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJiacun_Double-Fourth_Temple_Festival_in_May_2016_02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Thni_Kong_Tnua%2C_Air_Itam%2C_Penang.jpg/500px-Thni_Kong_Tnua%2C_Air_Itam%2C_Penang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Thni_Kong_Tnua%2C_Air_Itam%2C_Penang.jpg/1280px-Thni_Kong_Tnua%2C_Air_Itam%2C_Penang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Thni_Kong_Tnua%2C_Air_Itam%2C_Penang.jpg/500px-Thni_Kong_Tnua%2C_Air_Itam%2C_Penang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Thni Kong Tnua in Air Itam, Penang, Malaysia was specifically built in honor of the Jade Emperor.[12]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThni_Kong_Tnua%2C_Air_Itam%2C_Penang.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip